# Activity: Encrypted Journaling UI & Vitest Component Tests

## 1. Objective & Context
Implement the client-side UI for **RF04 — Encrypted Journaling** (`JournalView.vue`). Provide an uncluttered, distraction-free Markdown editor for personal reflections, a secure passphrase unlock modal, a mood selector, and write automated component tests using Vitest and Vue Test Utils.

- **Prerequisites:** Activities 01, 02, and 03 of Feature 09.
- **Target Location:** `frontend/src/views/JournalView.vue`, `frontend/src/components/journal/`, and `frontend/tests/`.

## 2. Technical Scope & Specifications
- **Editor:** Clean textarea or minimal Markdown editor with auto-save indicator.
- **Security Indicator:** Lock icon badge showing whether the client vault is `Locked` (red/gray) or `Decrypted & In-Memory` (green).
- **Testing Framework:** `vitest` (`2.x`) and `@vue/test-utils` (`2.4.x`).

## 3. Component Architecture

```
frontend/src/components/journal/
├── VaultUnlockModal.vue
├── JournalEditor.vue
├── MoodSelector.vue
├── TagInput.vue
└── LockStatusBadge.vue
```

### Vault Unlock Modal (`VaultUnlockModal.vue`)
```vue
<template>
  <div v-if="!isUnlocked" class="fixed inset-0 bg-black/80 backdrop-blur-sm flex items-center justify-center p-4 z-50">
    <div class="bg-surface-card border border-surface-border rounded-2xl max-w-md w-full p-6 space-y-4">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 text-white">
        <LockIcon class="w-6 h-6 text-brand-500" />
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold">Unlock Personal Journal</h3>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">
        Enter your master passphrase to decrypt your personal reflections locally. Your passphrase is never sent to the server.
      </p>
      <input
        v-model="passphrase"
        type="password"
        placeholder="Master Passphrase"
        class="w-full px-4 py-2 bg-surface-dark border border-surface-border rounded-lg text-white focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-brand-500"
        @keyup.enter="handleUnlock"
      />
      <button
        class="w-full py-2 bg-brand-600 hover:bg-brand-500 text-white font-medium rounded-lg transition"
        :disabled="isLoading"
        @click="handleUnlock"
      >
        {{ isLoading ? 'Deriving Keys...' : 'Unlock Journal' }}
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
</template>
```

## 4. Implementation Steps
1. Create `frontend/src/components/journal/` components.
2. Wire `WebCryptoService` into `handleUnlock` in `VaultUnlockModal.vue`:
   - Derive key in-memory via WASM Argon2id.
   - Set key in `useVaultStore`.
3. Implement `JournalEditor.vue`:
   - When user clicks "Save Reflection", call `WebCryptoService.encrypt()`.
   - Send pre-encrypted Base64 payload to `POST /api/v1/journal`.
4. Configure Vitest in `frontend/vite.config.ts`:
   ```typescript
   /// <reference types="vitest" />
   export default defineConfig({
     // ...
     test: {
       environment: 'jsdom',
       globals: true,
     },
   });
   ```
5. Write unit and component tests in `frontend/tests/journal.spec.ts`.

## 5. Security, Error Handling & Edge Cases
- **No Plaintext Network Traffic:** Verify in tests that the network request payload contains zero occurrences of the plaintext words entered in the textarea.
- **Auto-Wipe on Lock:** Clicking the "Lock Vault" button immediately resets the `CryptoKey` reference to `null` and clears the textarea.

## 6. Verification & Automated Tests
- Run Vitest:
  ```bash
  cd frontend && npm run test
  ```
- All test suites must pass.

## 7. Definition of Done (DoD)
- [ ] Journal UI components implemented with lock/unlock status indicators.
- [ ] Text is encrypted locally prior to dispatching HTTP mutation requests.
- [ ] Vitest component tests pass verifying encryption and vault locking.
